---
// Name, email, company, message. Submits via Netlify Forms (static HTML scan requires
// data-netlify="true" + matching name + hidden form-name input, present verbatim in
// the built output). Plain mailto fallback rendered near the form, not styled as a
// competing CTA (SPEC.md — ContactForm). Mailto/error-message address is the real
// business address, contact@xheia.co (Google Workspace on the xheia.co domain) - the
// actual Netlify Forms submission delivery address is separate, configured in
// Netlify's own dashboard (Site settings → Forms → Form notifications), not in code.
//
// Labels styled as $-prefixed prompts (terminal register, zero UX risk — pure
// markup/CSS, no new interaction) — all fields stay visible/editable at once, no
// step-by-step wizard, since a lead-capture form is the wrong place to trade
// usability for flair (entering-data.md favors efficient entry over sequencing).
//
// Progressive-enhancement submit handler: with JS, a fetch-based Netlify Forms
// submission shows a typed success confirmation (src/scripts/typewriter.ts) or an
// inline error — the site previously gave zero feedback after submission, a real
// risk for its one lead-gen action (feedback.md: "confirm that a significant
// action has completed"). With JS disabled, the form still submits via its native
// POST exactly as before, just without the inline confirmation.
//
// Book-a-call link, added in the booking-link-and-pricing-page pass (SPEC.md —
// ContactForm / Nav "Single CTAButton, one deliberate exception"): a second
// plain-text link at the same visual weight as the mailto fallback above it —
// deliberately not a second CTAButton style, not a competing CTA. Points to a
// public Google Calendar Appointment Schedule link (opens in a new tab since it
// leaves the site entirely, same convention as any other outbound link would
// warrant) — no sign-in required to view it, unlike a private week-view URL.
// Wrapped, along with the form and both status paragraphs, in one
// .contact-form-shell root: this component previously returned several
// top-level siblings with no wrapper, which is normally harmless — until
// contact.astro's two-column CSS grid treats each of THIS component's
// top-level elements as its own grid item. With a second mailto-style
// paragraph added, that split the two links across separate grid cells (the
// book-a-call line landing under the form, the mailto line landing under the
// unrelated left column) instead of stacking together under the form as
// intended. A single wrapper makes this component one grid item again,
// regardless of how many paragraphs it renders internally.
//
// Smoothness pass (explicit request - "drastic, no small changes," same treatment
// as About): fields previously appeared all at once with zero motion, and every
// interactive state (focus ring, button hover, the success/error swap) snapped
// instantly with no transition. Reworked with real deceleration easing
// (cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1), matching About) throughout: fields cascade in on
// load, the submit button gets a tactile press state, and the form->confirmation
// swap - the page's actual payoff moment per feedback.md's "confirm that a
// significant action has completed" - is now a coordinated crossfade (the form
// eases out, then the confirmation eases in with the same soft glow used on
// About's photo) instead of an abrupt cut. The JS checks prefers-reduced-motion
// directly (matchMedia) to skip the leave/enter choreography's timing entirely
// when motion is reduced, rather than relying on CSS alone to hide it.
---

<div class="contact-form-shell">
  <form
    name="contact"
    method="POST"
    data-netlify="true"
    data-netlify-honeypot="bot-field"
    class="contact-form"
    id="contact-form"
    data-reveal
  >
    <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="contact" />
    <p class="honeypot" aria-hidden="true">
      <label>
        Leave this field blank
        <input name="bot-field" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
      </label>
    </p>

    <label class="item-content" style={{ transitionDelay: '0s' }}>
      <span class="prompt"><span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">$</span> name</span>
      <input class="pixel-notch" type="text" name="name" placeholder="Your name" required />
    </label>

    <label class="item-content" style={{ transitionDelay: '0.1s' }}>
      <span class="prompt"><span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">$</span> email</span>
      <input class="pixel-notch" type="email" name="email" placeholder="name@company.com" required />
    </label>

    <label class="item-content" style={{ transitionDelay: '0.2s' }}>
      <span class="prompt">
        <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">$</span> company <span class="optional">(optional)</span>
      </span>
      <input class="pixel-notch" type="text" name="company" placeholder="Where you work" />
    </label>

    <label class="item-content" style={{ transitionDelay: '0.3s' }}>
      <span class="prompt"><span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">$</span> message</span>
      <textarea
        class="pixel-notch"
        name="message"
        rows="6"
        placeholder="What are you trying to solve?"
        required
      ></textarea>
    </label>

    <button class="pixel-notch item-content" style={{ transitionDelay: '0.4s' }} type="submit">Send</button>
  </form>

  <p class="form-status" id="form-status" role="status" hidden>
    <span class="status-mark" id="form-status-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span id="form-status-text"></span>
  </p>
  <p class="sr-only" id="form-status-announcer" aria-live="polite"></p>

  <p class="mailto-fallback">
    Prefer email? Write to <a href="mailto:contact@xheia.co">contact@xheia.co</a> directly.
  </p>
  <p class="mailto-fallback">
    Prefer to talk first? <a href="https://calendar.app.google/DdsSsKTNJierjQu89" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book a call &rarr;</a>
  </p>
</div>

<script>
  import { typeText } from '../scripts/typewriter';

  const wait = (ms: number) => new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, ms));
  const FORM_LEAVE_MS = 450;

  const prefersReducedMotion = () =>
    window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

  // Two rAFs, not one: the first lets the browser commit the class removal /
  // display change from this frame; only the second is guaranteed to happen
  // after that paint, so the .is-visible transition reliably has a "from" state
  // to animate away from instead of sometimes collapsing to a no-op.
  const nextPaint = () =>
    new Promise<void>((resolve) => requestAnimationFrame(() => requestAnimationFrame(() => resolve())));

  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', () => {
    const form = document.getElementById('contact-form');
    const status = document.getElementById('form-status');
    const statusMark = document.getElementById('form-status-mark');
    const statusText = document.getElementById('form-status-text');
    const announcer = document.getElementById('form-status-announcer');
    const button = form?.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('button[type="submit"]');

    form?.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      if (!(form instanceof HTMLFormElement) || !status || !statusMark || !statusText || !announcer || !button) {
        return;
      }

      button.disabled = true;
      button.textContent = 'Sending...';

      try {
        const params = new URLSearchParams();
        new FormData(form).forEach((value, key) => params.append(key, String(value)));

        const res = await fetch(window.location.pathname, {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },
          body: params.toString(),
        });
        if (!res.ok) throw new Error('submit failed');

        const message = "Got it - I'll reply within a couple of business days.";

        if (!prefersReducedMotion()) {
          form.classList.add('is-leaving');
          await wait(FORM_LEAVE_MS);
        }

        form.hidden = true;
        status.hidden = false;
        status.className = 'form-status success';
        statusMark.textContent = '✓';
        announcer.textContent = message;

        if (!prefersReducedMotion()) {
          await nextPaint();
          status.classList.add('is-visible');
        } else {
          status.classList.add('is-visible');
        }

        typeText(statusText, message);
      } catch {
        button.disabled = false;
        button.textContent = 'Send';
        const message = 'Something went wrong - try again, or email contact@xheia.co directly.';
        status.hidden = false;
        status.className = 'form-status error';
        statusMark.textContent = '';
        statusText.textContent = message;
        announcer.textContent = message;

        if (!prefersReducedMotion()) {
          await nextPaint();
        }
        status.classList.add('is-visible');
      }
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  /* Caps at the form's own 32rem so the mailto/book-a-call lines below it
     don't stretch to the full grid-column width and wrap at a noticeably
     wider measure than the form sitting directly above them. */
  .contact-form-shell {
    max-width: 32rem;
  }

  .contact-form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    max-width: 32rem;
    transition:
      opacity 0.45s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      transform 0.45s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  .contact-form[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .contact-form.is-leaving {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(-0.5rem) scale(0.98);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  /* Smooth, coordinated field entrance - see the top comment block. Higher
     specificity than the sitewide [data-reveal]/.item-content rules in
     global.css (steps() timing), so this overrides them without touching that
     shared file. */
  .contact-form[data-reveal] .item-content {
    transform: translateY(0.75rem);
    transition:
      opacity 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      transform 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  .contact-form[data-reveal].is-visible .item-content {
    transform: none;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .contact-form {
      transition: none;
    }

    .contact-form.is-leaving {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
    }

    .contact-form[data-reveal] .item-content {
      transform: none;
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  .honeypot,
  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  label {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .prompt {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-1);
  }

  /* --accent-primary-text, not --accent-primary: same full-audit finding
     fixed sitewide - raw --accent-primary as text is 4.22:1 against Ink in
     dark mode, below the 4.5:1 minimum. */
  .glyph {
    color: var(--accent-primary-text);
  }

  .optional {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* Round two of the polish pass (direct feedback: still didn't read as "sleek" -
     a hover border wasn't the actual problem). The real issue: background was
     var(--bg), identical to the page itself, so a field was only ever a thin outline
     with nothing behind it - it never read as its own surface, resting or not.
     A barely-there tint (color-mix toward --text, works in both themes without a
     separate light-mode override since it's relative to whichever --bg is active)
     gives every field real presence at rest, not just on interaction. Padding
     bumped up too - the old spacing read as cramped/default-form-ish next to the
     rest of the site's generous spacing scale. */
  input,
  textarea {
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 5%, var(--bg));
    color: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 1rem;
    transition:
      background-color 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      box-shadow 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      border-color 0.35s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  input::placeholder,
  textarea::placeholder {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Fields had a focus ring but zero feedback before that - the first sign a field
     was interactive was clicking into it. A hover-only border tint + a slightly
     stronger fill (no ring - that's reserved for the accessibility-required focus
     state below) signals "this is ready" earlier. */
  input:hover,
  textarea:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent-primary);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 8%, var(--bg));
  }

  /* clip-path (.pixel-notch) cuts two corners off each field, so an outward `outline`/
     `box-shadow` would get clipped away right where it's cut. An inset ring stays
     inside the clipped shape instead. */
  input:focus-visible,
  textarea:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--text) 8%, var(--bg));
    border-color: var(--accent-primary);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--accent-primary);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    input,
    textarea {
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  textarea {
    resize: vertical;
  }

  button[type='submit'] {
    align-self: flex-start;
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent-primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--accent-primary);
    color: var(--on-accent-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    cursor: pointer;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 transparent;
    transition:
      opacity 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      box-shadow 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      transform 0.2s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  button[type='submit']:disabled {
    cursor: default;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  /* Polish pass: the same soft accent-primary bloom now on every other button on
     the site (CTAButton, the logo, the theme toggle) - this one was still opacity-
     dim only. :not(:disabled) so a disabled Send never glows on hover. */
  button[type='submit']:hover:not(:disabled),
  button[type='submit']:focus-visible {
    opacity: 0.85;
    box-shadow: 0 0 1rem -0.2rem color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-primary) 55%, transparent);
  }

  /* Light mode needs a materially bolder glow than the dark-mode value to read as a
     real bloom against Paper (Weber-Fechner - the same percentage shift is obvious
     near black, nearly imperceptible near white) - same finding as every other glow
     on the site, verified rather than guessed. */
  :global(html[data-theme='light']) button[type='submit']:hover:not(:disabled),
  :global(html[data-theme='light']) button[type='submit']:focus-visible {
    box-shadow: 0 0 1.25rem 0 color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-primary) 85%, transparent);
  }

  button[type='submit']:active:not(:disabled) {
    transform: scale(0.96);
  }

  button[type='submit']:disabled:hover {
    opacity: 0.6;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 transparent;
  }

  /* Same clip-path corner issue as inputs above — inset ring instead of outline.
     Combined with the outward glow above (two box-shadow layers, comma-separated)
     rather than replacing it - the inset ring is the accessibility-required
     indicator, the outward glow is the same decorative bloom every hover state
     gets. */
  button[type='submit']:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 2px var(--on-accent-primary),
      0 0 1rem -0.2rem color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-primary) 55%, transparent);
  }

  :global(html[data-theme='light']) button[type='submit']:focus-visible {
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 2px var(--on-accent-primary),
      0 0 1.25rem 0 color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-primary) 85%, transparent);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    button[type='submit'] {
      transition: opacity 0.3s ease;
    }

    button[type='submit']:active:not(:disabled) {
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  /* No border - matching the "zero borders anywhere" standard already applied
     everywhere else. The success state's own glow (box-shadow below) still
     marks it as a distinct moment; the error state relies on spacing alone,
     same as every other de-boxed element on the site now does. */
  .form-status {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    max-width: 32rem;
    padding: var(--space-4) 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(0.75rem);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 transparent;
    transition:
      opacity 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      transform 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      box-shadow 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
    --success-glow: 0 0 2.5rem -0.6rem color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-status) 45%, transparent);
  }

  /* Same light-mode boost as About's photo glow and the CTA glow - a colored
     box-shadow blur reads far weaker against a light surrounding than against
     black, independent of the color-mix percentage. */
  :global(html[data-theme='light']) .form-status {
    --success-glow: 0 0 3rem -0.2rem color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-status) 85%, transparent);
  }

  .form-status[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .form-status.is-visible {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: none;
  }

  .form-status.success {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .form-status.success.is-visible {
    box-shadow: var(--success-glow);
  }

  .form-status.error {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .form-status {
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  .status-mark {
    color: var(--accent-status);
  }

  /* Flare coral (light mode's --accent-status) is too low-contrast as small text —
     same fix already applied to PillarBlock/Capabilities/Hero's checkmarks. */
  :global(html[data-theme='light']) .status-mark {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .mailto-fallback {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  /* Two lines at the same visual weight, grouped as one small block rather
     than two independently-spaced statements - the book-a-call link is a
     second option next to the mailto fallback, not a separate paragraph. */
  .mailto-fallback + .mailto-fallback {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .mailto-fallback a {
    color: var(--accent-primary-text);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: transparent;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    transition: text-decoration-color 0.3s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  .mailto-fallback a:hover,
  .mailto-fallback a:focus-visible {
    text-decoration-color: currentColor;
  }

  .mailto-fallback a:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent-primary-text);
    outline-offset: 0.2em;
  }
</style>
